    helpSearchPh: 'Search: category, exclusion, SoA, NIS2, undo…', helpTopics: 'Topics', helpSteps: 'Getting started', readGuide: 'Read guide', helpNoRes: 'No results', helpNoResTxt: 'Try other words or check the glossary.', helpRes: (n) => `${n} result${n === 1 ? '' : 's'}`,
    helpGroups: [
      ['start', 'rocket', 'Getting started', 'What Rosetta is, what you need and where to start.', [
        ['What is Rosetta?', 'A tool that links the requirements of the **ENS**, **ISO/IEC 27001**, **NIS2**, **ISO/IEC 42001** and **Part-IS** (aviation) to 119 unified controls, and takes custom frameworks. You record each control once and Rosetta calculates compliance per framework, the gaps and the implementation order.'],
        ['Do I need to install anything?', 'No. It runs in the browser, with no server or account. Use the published version or download the `dist/` folder from the repository and open `index.html`.'],
        ['Where do I start?', 'From **Home**: create a project with your data, import the ENS SoA from Excel or open a sample case. Then set the **Scope** and record the status of the controls.'],
        ['Are the sample cases real?', 'No. They are six fictitious organisations. You can edit them; changes only affect your copy and **Reset** restores the original.']]],
      ['scope', 'compass', 'Scope and frameworks', 'Regulatory profile, ENS category, NIS2 applicability, Part-IS, custom frameworks and exclusions.', [
        ['What is the regulatory profile?', 'A few questions about where the organisation operates and what it is (public sector, supplier to the public sector, financial entity, aviation, AI, manufacturer). Rosetta proposes for each framework whether it is **mandatory**, **to be confirmed**, **contractual or voluntary** or **not applicable**, with its legal basis. You decide what goes into scope and record the reason, which appears in the reports. The engine proposes; it does not rule.'],
        ['What does it cover of Part-IS?', 'The 13 organisation requirements (points .200 to .260) of Implementing Regulation (EU) 2023/203 (IS.I.OR) and Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1645 (IS.D.OR), which share their structure. The mappings are the author’s judgement and never go beyond partial: Part-IS measures the impact on aviation safety. Requirements cannot be excluded one by one; only the full derogation of point .200 e exists.'],
        ['Can I load my own framework?', 'Yes: a corporate policy, a customer’s requirements, a tender or a standard you hold a licence for (for example IEC 62443 or ISO/IEC 20000). Import a “rosetta-marco” JSON or a CSV from **Scope**, review the mapping with the suggestions and Rosetta calculates its compliance like any other framework. The text never leaves your browser.'],
        ['How is the ENS category set?', 'By the levels of the **D, I, C, A and T** dimensions. If you declare a category lower than the levels imply, Rosetta uses the higher one, as Annex I of RD 311/2022 requires.'],
        ['How do I know whether NIS2 applies?', 'In **Scope**, the assistant applies arts. 2 and 3 of Directive (EU) 2022/2555 by sector, size and special cases: DNS, TLD registries, trust service providers, electronic communications, public administration, critical entities (CER), financial entities under DORA and the exclusions of art. 2.7–2.8.'],
        ['What does ISO/IEC 42001 cover?', 'Clauses 4 to 10 and the 38 Annex A controls. AI system impact assessment, data governance and intended use are not inherited from any security framework.'],
        ['Can I exclude a requirement?', 'Yes, from its detail panel and with a justification. Clauses 4 to 10 of ISO/IEC 27001 and ISO/IEC 42001, the obligations of NIS2 arts. 20, 21 and 23 and the Part-IS requirements cannot be excluded. In the ENS, whatever the level does not require shows as **not required**.']]],
      ['controls', 'layers', 'Controls and coverage', 'Unified controls, states and how coverage is calculated.', [
        ['What is a unified control?', 'A practice implemented once, for example "Multi-factor authentication", linked to the requirements it covers in each framework.'],
        ['How is a requirement’s coverage calculated?', 'It is the weighted average of its controls: implemented 1, partial 0.5, pending or not applicable 0. Each link weighs 1 if equivalent and 0.5 if partial.'],
        ['Why is a requirement partial with everything implemented?', 'Because all its controls have partial links. Coverage then cannot exceed **50 %**: a control that covers it fully is needed.'],
        ['Can I undo a change?', 'Yes. Press **Undo** in the notice or use `Ctrl + Z`; `Ctrl + Shift + Z` redoes. Thirty steps are kept and the history is cleared when you switch project.']]],
      ['eq', 'waypoints', 'Equivalences', 'Where the mappings come from and how to read them.', [
        ['Are the mappings official?', 'Only ENS ↔ ISO/IEC 27001 follows an official guide (CCN-STIC 825). The rest is the author’s judgement, checked against ENISA technical guidance; Part-IS mappings never go beyond partial. Review it with your auditor.'],
        ['What do full, partial and relation mean?', '**Full**: the control covers the requirement. **Partial**: it covers part of it and another control is needed. **Relation**: useful context that does not count towards coverage.'],
        ['Why does a requirement depend on several controls?', 'Because each framework groups things differently. ENS op.exp.7, for example, asks for a complete incident process, which Rosetta splits into plan, classification, response, lessons learned and reporting.'],
        ['What is the overlap between frameworks?', 'The share of one framework that would be covered by implementing every control another framework requires with a full link. It is a starting estimate, not an audit result.']]],
      ['gaps', 'shield-alert', 'Gaps and plan', 'Uncovered requirements, inconsistencies and work order.', [
        ['What is the difference between a gap and an inconsistency?', 'A **gap** is an applicable requirement with zero coverage. An **inconsistency** is a conflict between frameworks or data, such as an exclusion another framework does not allow or an implemented control without evidence.'],
        ['How is the action plan ordered?', 'By the requirements each pending control covers across all frameworks in scope. Moving a card to **Done** marks the control as implemented.'],
        ['Can I turn off consistency rules?', 'Yes, in **Settings → Consistency review**. Disabled rules do not appear in Gaps or in reports.']]],
      ['io', 'file-spreadsheet', 'Import and export', 'ENS SoA, Excel, reports and backups.', [
        ['What format should the ENS SoA have?', 'An Excel workbook with a sheet containing the columns **Código** and **¿Aplica?**. If present, **Estado de implantación**, **% implantación**, **Justificación**, **Evidencias** and **Responsable** are also read; a sheet with columns **ID, D, I, C, A, T** provides the levels. The ENS Compliance Studio JSON is also accepted.'],
        ['What does the exported Excel include?', 'Summary, controls, one Statement of Applicability per framework, the crosswalk, the consistency review and the action plan, with author and date.'],
        ['How do I move my projects to another computer?', 'In **Settings → Backup** download a JSON with profile, settings and every project. On the other computer, use **Restore**.']]],
      ['data', 'shield-check', 'Data and privacy', 'Where data is stored and what precautions to take.', [
        ['Where is my data stored?', 'Only in this browser’s local storage, unencrypted. Rosetta sends no data to any server and uses no accounts, third-party cookies or analytics.'],
        ['Can I use the published version with real data?', 'With care: every page on the same GitHub Pages domain shares storage. For client data, use a local copy or your own domain, and avoid shared computers.'],
        ['What happens if I clear the browser data?', 'The projects are lost. Download backups regularly.'],
        ['Is NIS2 already mandatory in Spain?', 'The Directive is in force, but as of October 2026 the Spanish transposition law is still going through parliament. Rosetta applies the Directive’s criteria.']]]
    ],
