    steps: [['Create or open a project', 'Start with your data, import your ENS SoA or open one of the six cases.', 'inicio'], ['Define the scope', 'Answer the regulatory profile, confirm which frameworks apply and why, and adjust the ENS and NIS2.', 'alcance'], ['Record control status', 'Each control is set once and counts for every framework that requires it.', 'controles'], ['Check equivalences', 'Select a requirement to see its equivalents in the other frameworks.', 'traductor'], ['Review gaps', 'Uncovered requirements and inconsistencies, sorted by severity.', 'brechas'], ['Export', 'Excel with one SoA per framework, Markdown report and CSV plan.', 'exportar']],
    go: 'Go', search2: 'Search a term…', rule: 'Rule', severity: 'Severity', checks: 'What it checks', inProject: 'In this project',
    methodP1: (c, d) => `Frameworks are not compared with each other directly: all of them link to ${c} unified controls in ${d} domains. One-to-one crosswalk tables treat a requirement as met when a similar one exists in another framework; this model avoids that.`,
    methodCards: [['Three kinds of link', 'Full (weight 1), partial (weight 0.5: it contributes a part and another control is needed) and informative relation (does not count).'], ['Requirement coverage', 'Weighted average of its controls: implemented 1, partial 0.5, pending 0. Covered at 100 %; gap at 0. A requirement with only partial links cannot exceed 50 %.'], ['Priority', 'Each pending control is scored by the requirements it covers across every framework in scope.']],
    methodSrc: 'Sources: RD 311/2022 (Annex II); ISO/IEC 27001:2022; Directive (EU) 2022/2555, arts. 20, 21 and 23; Implementing Regulation (EU) 2024/2690; ENISA technical guidance (June 2025); ISO/IEC 42001:2023; Implementing Regulation (EU) 2023/203 and Delegated Regulation (EU) 2022/1645 (Part-IS), as amended. ISO/IEC titles are cited in abbreviated form for reference only: the text of ISO standards is copyrighted and is not reproduced.',
    methodVal: (p, t, r) => `Validation: the map reproduces ${p} of the ${t} ENS ↔ ISO/IEC 27001 equivalences in the reference SoA template; another ${r} appear as informative relations.`,
    methodCcn: (ed, m, p, a, pa, n, pr) => `ENS ↔ ISO/IEC 27001 equivalences aligned with the National Cryptologic Centre guide CCN-STIC 825 (${ed === 'abril 2026' ? 'April 2026' : ed}): ${m} Annex II measures with their main control, complementary controls and compatibility level (${a} analogous, ${pa} partially analogous and ${n} with no ISO equivalent). The strength of each equivalence comes from the guide: analogous main control, full; partially analogous or complementary, partial; measure without equivalent or “other controls”, related. The ${pr} ENS ↔ ISO equivalences not in the guide are flagged as own criterion and never exceed partial. NIS2 and ISO/IEC 42001 remain own-criterion mappings. This alignment is a correction in version 2.3.0, made after an external review received once Rosetta was published; up to 2.2.0 these equivalences were own criterion.`,
    methodOv: 'Overlap between frameworks (if you implement everything the row requires, how much of the column you cover):',
    keys: [['Ctrl / ⌘ + K', 'Search requirements, controls and actions'], ['[', 'Collapse or expand the side menu'], ['/', 'Search in the current view'], ['Ctrl / ⌘ + Z', 'Undo the last change'], ['Ctrl / ⌘ + Shift + Z', 'Redo'], ['Esc', 'Close panels and menus'], ['?', 'Open help'], ['G then O', 'Go to Overview'], ['G then P', 'Go to Equivalences'], ['G then C', 'Go to Controls'], ['G then B', 'Go to Gaps']],
    glosario: [['Unified control', 'A practice implemented once (e.g. "Multi-factor authentication") that covers requirements of several frameworks.'], ['Full link', 'The control covers the requirement, or its share together with other full controls.'], ['Partial link', 'The control contributes a part and another control is also needed. Weighs half.'], ['Informative relation', 'Related to the requirement but not needed to meet it. Does not count.'], ['Coverage', 'Weighted average of the state of the controls supporting a requirement.'], ['Gap', 'Applicable requirement whose support is entirely pending.'], ['Overlap', 'Share of one framework that would be covered by implementing every control another framework requires.'], ['ENS', 'Spanish National Security Framework (RD 311/2022): 73 measures required by system category.'], ['ISO/IEC 27001:2022', 'Certifiable information security management standard: clauses 4–10 and 93 controls.'], ['NIS2', 'Directive (EU) 2022/2555: essential and important entities, art. 21 measures and art. 23 reporting.'], ['IR 2024/2690', 'Implementing Regulation with NIS2 technical requirements for digital providers; a practical reference for others.'], ['ISO/IEC 42001:2023', 'Certifiable AI management system standard: clauses 4–10 and 38 controls.'], ['Statement of Applicability', 'Which controls apply and why; required by the ENS, ISO/IEC 27001 and ISO/IEC 42001.'], ['AI impact assessment', 'Consequences of an AI system for individuals, groups and society. Not inherited from any security framework.']],
